WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.246
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.546 --> 00:00:09.246
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.546 --> 00:00:15.321
Unit seventeen: My Best Friend. Today you will describe your best friend and your friendship habits.

4
00:00:15.621 --> 00:00:18.401
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:22.634
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:24.566
Best friend.

7
00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.828
Best friend means the friend you like most.

8
00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:30.172
Dara is my best friend.

9
00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:33.447
Your turn. Say: Best friend.

10
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.545
Best friend.

11
00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:39.075
Trust.

12
00:00:40.083 --> 00:00:43.000
Trust means to believe someone is honest and good.

13
00:00:43.617 --> 00:00:45.221
I trust him completely.

14
00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:48.028
Your turn. Say: Trust.

15
00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:51.519
Trust.

16
00:00:52.283 --> 00:00:53.157
Loyal.

17
00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.498
Loyal means always supporting a friend.

18
00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:59.071
A loyal friend never leaves you.

19
00:00:59.683 --> 00:01:01.999
Your turn. Say: Loyal.

20
00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:05.753
Loyal.

21
00:01:06.517 --> 00:01:07.564
Support.

22
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:10.886
Support means to help and encourage someone.

23
00:01:11.483 --> 00:01:13.216
She supports me when I'm sad.

24
00:01:13.817 --> 00:01:16.295
Your turn. Say: Support.

25
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:19.995
Support.

26
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:21.751
Honest.

27
00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:25.121
Honest means always telling the truth.

28
00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:27.972
My best friend is always honest with me.

29
00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:31.340
Your turn. Say: Honest.

30
00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.039
Honest.

31
00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:36.483
Share.

32
00:01:37.483 --> 00:01:40.203
Share means to let others have or use something too.

33
00:01:40.817 --> 00:01:42.004
We share our lunch.

34
00:01:42.617 --> 00:01:45.234
Your turn. Say: Share.

35
00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:48.927
Share.

36
00:01:49.683 --> 00:01:50.742
Understand.

37
00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:54.260
Understand means to know how someone feels.

38
00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.977
She understands me without words.

39
00:01:57.583 --> 00:02:00.050
Your turn. Say: Understand.

40
00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:03.913
Understand.

41
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:05.454
Close.

42
00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.809
Close means having a strong friendship.

43
00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:11.242
We have been close since Grade 1.

44
00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:14.096
Your turn. Say: Close.

45
00:02:16.933 --> 00:02:17.772
Close.

46
00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:21.950
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.817 --> 00:02:24.886
Visal, who is your best friend?

48
00:02:25.983 --> 00:02:30.331
My best friend is Rathana. We sit together every day.

49
00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:32.824
What do you do together?

50
00:02:33.917 --> 00:02:37.716
We always share our snacks, and we often study together.

51
00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:40.352
Why do you trust him?

52
00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:45.414
He is honest and loyal. He always supports me.

53
00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.288
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:52.485
Grammar focus: Present simple for habits.

55
00:02:52.785 --> 00:02:53.890
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:54.583 --> 00:02:56.722
My best friend always supports me.

57
00:02:57.617 --> 00:02:58.862
We share everything.

58
00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:01.471
We often study together.

59
00:03:02.433 --> 00:03:05.861
Use the present simple for things that are true or happen regularly.

60
00:03:06.617 --> 00:03:10.755
Be careful! Don't say: My best friend always support me.

61
00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:15.710
Say: My best friend always supports me.

62
00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:18.288
Add -s to the verb with he, she and it.

63
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.973
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:23.954
A True Friend.

65
00:03:24.254 --> 00:03:27.124
My best friend and I trust each other completely.

66
00:03:28.133 --> 00:03:30.713
We are loyal and always support one another.

67
00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.617
We share our secrets and problems because we are honest.

68
00:03:35.633 --> 00:03:38.422
When I'm sad, my best friend understands me.

69
00:03:39.433 --> 00:03:42.803
We have been close for many years, and I hope we always will be.

70
00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:48.029
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:48.883 --> 00:03:50.709
My friend always blank me.

72
00:03:51.009 --> 00:03:54.325
A, helps. B, help. C, helping.

73
00:03:57.867 --> 00:03:59.727
The answer is A: helps.

74
00:04:00.883 --> 00:04:03.022
Always telling the truth is blank.

75
00:04:03.322 --> 00:04:07.115
A, honest. B, loyal. C, close.

76
00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:12.759
The answer is A: honest.

77
00:04:13.917 --> 00:04:16.775
To believe someone is honest and good is to blank them.

78
00:04:17.075 --> 00:04:20.648
A, trust. B, share. C, support.

79
00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.991
The answer is A: trust.

80
00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.177
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:31.017 --> 00:04:32.947
What makes someone a good best friend?

82
00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.796
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:44.096 --> 00:04:50.522
A good best friend is honest and loyal. My best friend always supports me, and we share everything.

84
00:04:50.822 --> 00:04:52.566
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:57.937
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present simple for habits.

86
00:04:58.237 --> 00:05:02.805
Today's value is loyalty. Stand by your friends in good times and bad times.

87
00:05:03.105 --> 00:05:05.780
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

88
00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.570
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

